# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context exclusions
#
# The primary goal here is to keep the context small so `docker build` doesn't
# stream hundreds of MB (or GB) to the daemon on every build. Anything the
# Dockerfile does not COPY belongs here.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── Dependency directories (huge, rebuilt inside the image) ──────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
venv
**/venv
.pnp
.pnp.js

# ── Build output (regenerated inside the image) ──────────────────────────────
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
dist
**/dist
build
**/build

# ── Python bytecode / caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info

# ── Local databases & mutable runtime state ─────────────────────────────────-
db.sqlite3
**/db.sqlite3
db/
logs/
**/logs/
logs.txt
**/logs.txt

# ── Environment / secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!env.example

# ── Version control & IDE metadata ───────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea
.vscode
.claude

# ── Developer-only content not needed at runtime ─────────────────────────────
imageFolder/
mockData/
devTO.md
README.md
client/intellihunt/README.md
server/README.md
.github

# ── Docker files themselves ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yaml
docker-compose*.yml

# ── Platform / OS junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo

# ── CrewAI runtime caches (regenerated per container) ────────────────────────
crewai-rag-tool.lock
**/crewai-rag-tool.lock
chroma.sqlite3
**/chroma.sqlite3
# Stale ChromaDB state under crew/db — contents are regenerated on use.
server/intelliHunt/crew/db/
